{"case_id":"T8042","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","input semantics","configuration/state","attack surface","harness build compatibility"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["h2o_qpack_flatten_request","start_request","tunnel_on_udp_sock_read","tunnel_on_udp_read","handle_input_expect_data_frame","h2o_httpclient_connect","h2o_httpclient__connect_h3"],"reason":"H0 only generates a fixed GET-over-HTTPS HEADERS frame and cannot exercise the new extended-CONNECT/CONNECT-UDP behavior. S1 adds a `protocol` argument to `h2o_qpack_flatten_request` and conditionally emits `H2O_TOKEN_PROTOCOL`, but H0 neither supplies that argument nor varies method, scheme, upgrade state, or protocol. It also cannot reach the new RFC9298 datagram framing paths controlled by `connect_udp_is_rfc9298`. Those paths process attacker-controlled datagram lengths, and `tunnel_on_udp_read` subtracts a one-byte context ID from `src->len` without first checking that `src->len >= 1`, making short datagrams especially fuzz-worthy. As written, H0's old `h2o_qpack_flatten_request` call is also incompatible with S1's changed public signature.","evidence":["S1 changes `h2o_qpack_flatten_request` to accept `h2o_iovec_t protocol` between `path` and `headers`, while H0 still passes `headers.entries` immediately after `path`.","`h2o_qpack_flatten_request` now emits `H2O_TOKEN_PROTOCOL` when `protocol.base != NULL`; H0 fixes the method to `GET`, scheme to `H2O_URL_SCHEME_HTTPS`, and has no protocol input.","`start_request` sets `protocol` only when `req->super.upgrade_to == h2o_httpclient_upgrade_to_connect_udp`, a newly accepted state in `h2o_httpclient__connect_h3` and `h2o_httpclient_connect`.","The new `--connect-udp-rfc-version` configuration selects `rfc9298` versus `draft03`, changes CONNECT-UDP into `CONNECT`, constructs `/.well-known/masque/udp/...`, adds `capsule-protocol: ?1`, and changes datagram context-ID handling; none of these states exist in H0.","In `tunnel_on_udp_read`, RFC9298 mode sets `context_id_len` to 1 and constructs a vector using `src->base + context_id_len` and `src->len - context_id_len` without validating `src->len`, so a zero-length datagram can underflow the length.","`handle_input_expect_data_frame` now rejects a HEADERS frame whenever `req->super.upgrade_to != NULL`, broadening response-state behavior that a header-generation-only harness does not exercise."],"recommended_action":"Update the QPACK harness for S1's signature and make `method`, `scheme`, `path`, `protocol`, headers, and datagram-flow ID fuzz-controlled, including valid and invalid `CONNECT` plus `connect-udp` combinations. Add a stateful HTTP/3 client/datagram harness that toggles draft03/RFC9298 behavior, drives `upgrade_to`, response frame sequencing, and zero-, one-, and multi-byte incoming datagrams through `tunnel_on_udp_read` and related callbacks."}
